{"id":"mahabharata-9-016","work":"mahabharata","part":9,"partName":"शल्यपर्व","partNameEn":"Shalya Parva","unit":16,"title":"षोडशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 16 · Yudhishthira kills Shalya","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira, taking another bow, fights Shalya furiously, and at last hurls the blazing spear that pierces Shalya's heart, killing the king of Madra. Shalya's younger brother attacks and is also slain, and the Pandavas praise Yudhishthira.","kn":"ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರ ಇನ್ನೊಂದು ಬಿಲ್ಲು ಹಿಡಿದು ಶಲ್ಯನೊಡನೆ ಉಗ್ರವಾಗಿ ಹೋರಾಡಿ ಕೊನೆಗೆ ಉರಿಯುವ ಶಕ್ತಿ ಎಸೆದು ಶಲ್ಯನ ಹೃದಯ ಭೇದಿಸಿ ಮದ್ರರಾಜನನ್ನು ಕೊಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಶಲ್ಯನ ತಮ್ಮ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡಿ ಹತನಾಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಪಾಂಡವರು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನನ್ನು ಹೊಗಳುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर दूसरा धनुष लेकर शल्य से उग्र युद्ध करते हैं और अन्त में जलती शक्ति फेंककर शल्य का हृदय बींध देते हैं, मद्रराज मारा जाता है। शल्य का छोटा भाई आक्रमण कर मारा जाता है, और पाण्डव युधिष्ठिर की प्रशंसा करते हैं।","te":"యుధిష్ఠిరుడు మరో విల్లు తీసుకుని శల్యునితో ఉగ్రంగా పోరాడి చివరికి మండే శక్తిని విసిరి శల్యుని గుండెను ఛేదించి మద్రరాజును చంపుతాడు. శల్యుని తమ్ముడు దాడి చేసి చంపబడతాడు; పాండవులు యుధిష్ఠిరుని ప్రశంసిస్తారు.","ta":"யுதிஷ்டிரர் வேறு வில்லை எடுத்துச் சல்யனுடன் கடும்போர் புரிந்து இறுதியில் எரியும் வேலை எறிந்து சல்யனின் இதயத்தைத் துளைத்து மத்ர மன்னனைக் கொல்கிறார். சல்யனின் தம்பி தாக்கிக் கொல்லப்பட, பாண்டவர் யுதிஷ்டிரரைப் புகழ்கின்றனர்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ മറ്റൊരു വില്ലെടുത്ത് ശല്യനോട് കോപത്തോടെ പൊരുതുന്നു; ഒടുവിൽ ജ്വലിക്കുന്ന കുന്തമെറിഞ്ഞ് അത് ശല്യന്റെ ഹൃദയം തുളയ്ക്കുന്നു; മദ്രരാജാവ് മരിക്കുന്നു. ശല്യന്റെ അനുജൻ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നതും അദ്ദേഹവും കൊല്ലപ്പെടുന്നതും സംഭവിക്കുന്നു; പാണ്ഡവർ യുധിഷ്ഠിരനെ പ്രശംസിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 9.16; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jun 23 2020","sections":[{"title":"शल्यपर्व","titleEn":"Shalya Parva","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अथान्यद्धनुरादाय बलवद्वेगवत्तरम् ।\nयुधिष्ठिरं मद्रपतिर्विद्ध्वा सिंह इवानदत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of Madra took another, stronger and swifter bow, pierced Yudhishthira, and roared like a lion."}},{"n":2,"text":"ततः स शरवर्षेण पर्जन्य इव वृष्टिमान् ।\nअभ्यवर्षदमेयात्मा क्षत्रियान्क्षत्रियर्षभः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then that man of immeasurable spirit, best of kshatriyas, rained showers of arrows on the kshatriyas, like Parjanya raining."}},{"n":3,"text":"सात्यकिं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा भीमसेनं त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nसहदेवं त्रिभिर्विद्ध्वा युधिष्ठिरमपीडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He pierced Satyaki with ten arrows, Bhimasena with three, and Sahadeva with three, and harried Yudhishthira."}},{"n":4,"text":"तांस्तानन्यान्महेष्वासान्साश्वान्सरथकुञ्जरान् ।\nकुञ्जरान्कुञ्जरारोहानश्वानश्वप्रयायिनः ।\nरथांश्च रथिभिः सार्धं जघान रथिनां वरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of chariot-fighters killed other great archers, with their horses, chariots and elephants, elephants with their riders, horses with their horsemen, and chariots with their chariot-fighters."}},{"n":5,"text":"बाहूंश्चिच्छेद च तथा सायुधान्केतनानि च ।\nचकार च महीं योधैस्तीर्णां वेदीं कुशैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"He cut off arms with their weapons and banners, and made the earth, strewn with warriors, like a sacrificial altar spread with kusha grass."}},{"n":6,"text":"तथा तमरिसैन्यानि घ्नन्तं मृत्युमिवान्तकम् ।\nपरिवव्रुर्भृशं क्रुद्धाः पाण्डुपाञ्चालसोमकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he struck down the enemy's troops like Death the Ender, the furious Pandavas, Panchalas and Somakas closed hard around him."}},{"n":7,"text":"तं भीमसेनश्च शिनेश्च नप्ता\nमाद्र्याश्च पुत्रौ पुरुषप्रवीरौ ।\nसमागतं भीमबलेन राज्ञा\nपर्यापुरन्योन्यमथाह्वयन्तः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena, Shini's grandson Satyaki, and the two sons of Madri, bravest of men, gathered about the king of Madras, whose strength matched Bhima's, challenging each other."}},{"n":8,"text":"ततस्तु शूराः समरे नरेन्द्रं\nमद्रेश्वरं प्राप्य युधां वरिष्ठम् ।\nआवार्य चैनं समरे नृवीरा\nजघ्नुः शरैः पत्रिभिरुग्रवेगैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the brave men, having reached the lord of Madra, the best of fighters, surrounded him in the battle and struck him with fierce, swift feathered arrows."}},{"n":9,"text":"संरक्षितो भीमसेनेन राजा\nमाद्रीसुताभ्यामथ माधवेन ।\nमद्राधिपं पत्रिभिरुग्रवेगैः\nस्तनान्तरे धर्मसुतो निजघ्ने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Guarded by Bhimasena, the two sons of Madri and Madhava, the son of Dharma struck the lord of Madra between the breasts with fierce, swift feathered arrows."}},{"n":10,"text":"ततो रणे तावकानां रथौघाः\nसमीक्ष्य मद्राधिपतिं शरार्तम् ।\nपर्यावव्रुः प्रवराः सर्वशश्च\nदुर्योधनस्यानुमते समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, seeing the lord of Madra hurt by arrows, the best of your chariot divisions closed in on every side in the battle, with Duryodhana's approval."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो द्रुतं मद्रजनाधिपो रणे\nयुधिष्ठिरं सप्तभिरभ्यविध्यत् ।\nतं चापि पार्थो नवभिः पृषत्कै-\nर्विव्याध राजंस्तुमुले महात्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king of the Madras quickly pierced Yudhishthira with seven arrows in the battle, and the great-souled Partha, O king, pierced him with nine in the tumult."}},{"n":12,"text":"आकर्णपूर्णायतसंप्रयुक्तैः\nशरैस्तदा संयति तैलधौतैः ।\nअन्योन्यमाच्छादयतां महारथौ\nमद्राधिपश्चापि युधिष्ठिरश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"With arrows well polished with oil, shot drawn to the ear, the two great warriors, the lord of Madra and Yudhishthira, covered each other in the fight."}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्तु तूर्णं समरे महारथौ\nपरस्परस्यान्तरमीक्षमाणौ ।\nशरैर्भृशं विव्यधतुर्नृपोत्तमौ\nमहाबलौ शत्रुभिरप्रधृष्यौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then those two great warriors, best of kings, strong and unassailable by enemies, quickly watching for each other's opening, pierced each other deeply with arrows."}},{"n":14,"text":"तयोर्धनुर्ज्यातलनिस्वनो महा-\nन्महेन्द्रवज्राशनितुल्यनिस्वनः ।\nपरस्परं बाणगणैर्महात्मनोः\nप्रवर्षतोर्मद्रपपाण्डुवीरयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great was the sound of their bowstrings and palms, like the crash of Indra's thunderbolt, as the two great-souled heroes, the Madra king and the Pandava, rained masses of arrows on each other."}},{"n":15,"text":"तौ चेरतुर्व्याघ्रशिशुप्रकाशौ\nमहावनेष्वामिषगृद्धिनाविव ।\nविषाणिनौ नागवराविवोभौ\nततक्षतुः संयुगजातदर्पौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They moved about like two tiger cubs hungry for meat in a great forest, and tore at each other like two great tusked elephants, proud from the fray."}},{"n":16,"text":"ततस्तु मद्राधिपतिर्महात्मा\nयुधिष्ठिरं भीमबलं प्रसह्य ।\nविव्याध वीरं हृदयेऽतिवेगं\nशरेण सूर्याग्निसमप्रभेण ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled lord of Madra, forcing it, pierced the hero Yudhishthira, strong as Bhima, very swiftly in the heart with an arrow bright as the sun and fire."}},{"n":17,"text":"ततोऽतिविद्धोऽथ युधिष्ठिरोऽपि\nसुसंप्रयुक्तेन शरेण राजन् ।\nजघान मद्राधिपतिं महात्मा\nमुदं च लेभे ऋषभः कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Deeply pierced, Yudhishthira too, O king, with a well-aimed arrow struck the lord of Madra, and that great-souled bull of the Kurus felt joy."}},{"n":18,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तादिव पार्थिवेन्द्रो\nलब्ध्वा संज्ञां क्रोधसंरक्तनेत्रः ।\nशतेन पार्थं त्वरितो जघान\nसहस्रनेत्रप्रतिमप्रभावः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, regaining his senses after a moment, his eyes red with rage, quickly struck Partha with a hundred arrows, with a power like the thousand-eyed Indra."}},{"n":19,"text":"त्वरंस्ततो धर्मसुतो महात्मा\nशल्यस्य क्रुद्धो नवभिः पृषत्कैः ।\nभित्त्वा ह्युरस्तपनीयं च वर्म\nजघान षड्भिस्त्वपरैः पृषत्कैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled son of Dharma, angry, hurrying, pierced Shalya's chest and golden armor with nine arrows and struck him with six more."}},{"n":20,"text":"ततस्तु मद्राधिपतिः प्रहृष्टो\nधनुर्विकृष्य व्यसृजत्पृषत्कान् ।\nद्वाभ्यां क्षुराभ्यां च तथैव राज्ञ-\nश्चिच्छेद चापं कुरुपुंगवस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the delighted lord of Madra drew his bow, loosed arrows, and with two razor-arrows cut the bow of the king, the bull of the Kurus."}},{"n":21,"text":"नवं ततोऽन्यत्समरे प्रगृह्य\nराजा धनुर्घोरतरं महात्मा ।\nशल्यं तु विद्ध्वा निशितैः समन्ता-\nद्यथा महेन्द्रो नमुचिं शिताग्रैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great-souled king took another, new and more fearsome bow in the battle and pierced Shalya all around with sharp arrows, as great Indra pierced Namuchi."}},{"n":22,"text":"ततस्तु शल्यो नवभिः पृषत्कै-\nर्भीमस्य राज्ञश्च युधिष्ठिरस्य ।\nनिकृत्य रौक्मे पटुवर्मणी तयो-\nर्विदारयामास भुजौ महात्मा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Shalya with nine arrows cut the strong armor of both Bhima and King Yudhishthira, and the great man tore at their arms."}},{"n":23,"text":"ततोऽपरेण ज्वलितार्कतेजसा\nक्षुरेण राज्ञो धनुरुन्ममाथ ।\nकृपश्च तस्यैव जघान सूतं\nषड्भिः शरैः सोऽभिमुखं पपात ॥","meaning":{"en":"With another razor-arrow bright as the blazing sun he shattered the king's bow, and Kripa killed his charioteer with six arrows; the man fell forward."}},{"n":24,"text":"मद्राधिपश्चापि युधिष्ठिरस्य\nशरैश्चतुर्भिर्निजघान वाहान् ।\nवाहांश्च हत्वा व्यकरोन्महात्मा\nयोधक्षयं धर्मसुतस्य राज्ञः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of Madra also killed Yudhishthira's horses with four arrows, and having killed the horses, that great-souled man brought about the destruction of the warriors of the king, the son of Dharma."}},{"n":25,"text":"तथा कृते राजनि भीमसेनो\nमद्राधिपस्याशु ततो महात्मा ।\nछित्त्वा धनुर्वेगवता शरेण\nद्वाभ्यामविध्यत्सुभृशं नरेन्द्रम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king was so served, great-souled Bhimasena quickly cut the lord of Madra's bow with a swift arrow and pierced the king very hard with two."}},{"n":26,"text":"अथापरेणास्य जहार यन्तुः\nकायाच्छिरः संनहनीयमध्यात् ।\nजघान चाश्वांश्चतुरः स शीघ्रं\nतथा भृशं कुपितो भीमसेनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With another he took the charioteer's head from his body, from the middle of his armor, and angry Bhimasena quickly killed his four horses as well."}},{"n":27,"text":"तमग्रणीः सर्वधनुर्धराणा-\nमेकं चरन्तं समरेऽतिवेगम् ।\nभीमः शतेन व्यकिरच्छराणां\nमाद्रीपुत्रः सहदेवस्तथैव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that foremost of all archers moved alone and very swiftly in the battle, Bhima scattered a hundred arrows over him, and Sahadeva, son of Madri, did the same."}},{"n":28,"text":"तैः सायकैर्मोहितं वीक्ष्य शल्यं\nभीमः शरैरस्य चकर्त वर्म ।\nस भीमसेनेन निकृत्तवर्मा\nमद्राधिपश्चर्म सहस्रतारम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Shalya dazed by those arrows, Bhima cut his armor with arrows; and the lord of Madra, his armor cut by Bhimasena, took a shield with a thousand moons,"}},{"n":29,"text":"प्रगृह्य खड्गं च रथान्महात्मा\nप्रस्कन्द्य कुन्तीसुतमभ्यधावत् ।\nछित्त्वा रथेषां नकुलस्य सोऽथ\nयुधिष्ठिरं भीमबलोऽभ्यधावत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and a sword, and the great-souled man leapt from his chariot and ran at the son of Kunti; cutting Nakula's chariot-pole on the way, that man of Bhima's strength rushed at Yudhishthira."}},{"n":30,"text":"तं चापि राजानमथोत्पतन्तं\nक्रुद्धं यथैवान्तकमापतन्तम् ।\nधृष्टद्युम्नो द्रौपदेयाः शिखण्डी\nशिनेश्च नप्ता सहसा परीयुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that king sprang up, angry like Death coming on, Dhrishtadyumna, the sons of Draupadi, Shikhandi and Shini's grandson swiftly surrounded him."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथास्य चर्माप्रतिमं न्यकृन्त-\nद्भीमो महात्मा दशभिः पृषत्कः ।\nखड्गं च भल्लैर्निचकर्त मुष्टौ\nनदन्प्रहृष्टस्तव सैन्यमध्ये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then great-souled Bhima with ten arrows cut his incomparable shield, and with broad-headed arrows cut the sword in his fist, roaring in delight in the midst of your army."}},{"n":32,"text":"तत्कर्म भीमस्य समीक्ष्य हृष्टा-\nस्ते पाण्डवानां प्रवरा रथौघाः ।\nनादं च चक्रुर्भृशमुत्स्मयन्तः\nशङ्खांश्च दध्मुः शशिसंनिकाशान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing that deed of Bhima, those best of Pandava chariot divisions rejoiced, and, smiling broadly, roared and blew their conches, white as the moon."}},{"n":33,"text":"तेनाथ शब्देन विभीषणेन\nतवाभितप्तं बलमप्रहृष्टम् ।\nस्वेदाभिभूतं रुधिरोक्षिताङ्गं\nविसंज्ञकल्पं च तथा विषण्णम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"At that terrifying noise your army, tormented and cheerless, drenched in sweat, its limbs wet with blood, was dazed, almost senseless, and despondent."}},{"n":34,"text":"स मद्रराजः सहसावकीर्णो\nभीमाग्रगैः पाण्डवयोधमुख्यैः ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्याभिमुखं जवेन\nसिंहो यथा मृगहेतोः प्रयातः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Suddenly scattered by the chief Pandava warriors led by Bhima, the king of Madras went swiftly toward Yudhishthira like a lion after prey."}},{"n":35,"text":"स धर्मराजो निहताश्वसूतं\nक्रोधेन दीप्तज्वलनप्रकाशम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा तु मद्राधिपतिं स तूर्णं\nसमभ्यधावत्तमरिं बलेन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the king of Madras, with his horses and charioteer dead, blazing like a lit fire with rage, the king of dharma quickly ran at that enemy with his force."}},{"n":36,"text":"गोविन्दवाक्यं त्वरितं विचिन्त्य\nदध्रे मतिं शल्यविनाशनाय ।\nस धर्मराजो निहताश्वसूते\nरथे तिष्ठञ्शक्तिमेवाभिकाङ्क्षन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Quickly thinking of Govinda's words, he set his mind on Shalya's destruction; the king of dharma, on a chariot whose horses and charioteer were dead, longed for a lance."}},{"n":37,"text":"तच्चापि शल्यस्य निशम्य कर्म\nमहात्मनो भागमथावशिष्टम् ।\nस्मृत्वा मनः शल्यवधे यतात्मा\nयथोक्तमिन्द्रावरजस्य चक्रे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing of that deed of the great-souled Shalya, and remembering the share that remained, self-controlled, he set his mind on Shalya's killing and did as the younger brother of Indra had said."}},{"n":38,"text":"स धर्मराजो मणिहेमदण्डां\nजग्राह शक्तिं कनकप्रकाशाम् ।\nनेत्रे च दीप्ते सहसा विवृत्य\nमद्राधिपं क्रुद्धमना निरैक्षत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The king of dharma took up a lance with a shaft of gems and gold, shining like gold, and suddenly opening his blazing eyes, looked at the lord of Madra with an angry mind."}},{"n":39,"text":"निरीक्षितो वै नरदेव राज्ञा\nपूतात्मना निर्हृतकल्मषेण ।\nअभून्न यद्भस्मसान्मद्रराज-\nस्तदद्भुतं मे प्रतिभाति राजन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Looked at, O king, by that king of pure soul, free of stain, the king of Madras was not reduced to ashes; that seems to me a wonder."}},{"n":40,"text":"ततस्तु शक्तिं रुचिरोग्रदण्डां\nमणिप्रवालोज्ज्वलितां प्रदीप्ताम् ।\nचिक्षेप वेगात्सुभृशं महात्मा\nमद्राधिपाय प्रवरः कुरूणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the great-souled foremost of the Kurus hurled with great force at the lord of Madra the lance, with its handsome, fierce shaft, bright with gems and coral and blazing."}},{"n":41,"text":"दीप्तामथैनां महता बलेन\nसविस्फुलिङ्गां सहसा पतन्तीम् ।\nप्रैक्षन्त सर्वे कुरवः समेता\nयथा युगान्ते महतीमिवोल्काम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the Kurus assembled saw it falling suddenly, blazing, with sparks, with great force, like a great meteor at the end of an age."}},{"n":42,"text":"तां कालरात्रीमिव पाशहस्तां\nयमस्य धात्रीमिव चोग्ररूपाम् ।\nसब्रह्मदण्डप्रतिमाममोघां\nससर्ज यत्तो युधि धर्मराजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, carefully hurled that unfailing weapon, like Kalaratri with a noose in her hand, like Yama's own nurse, fearsome, like Brahma's rod."}},{"n":43,"text":"गन्धस्रगग्र्यासनपानभोजनै-\nरभ्यर्चितां पाण्डुसुतैः प्रयत्नात् ।\nसंवर्तकाग्निप्रतिमां ज्वलन्तीं\nकृत्यामथर्वाङ्गिरसीमिवोग्राम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Pandavas had honored it with care with perfumes, garlands, the best seats, drink and food; it blazed like the fire of dissolution, like the fierce witchcraft of the Atharvangirasas."}},{"n":44,"text":"ईशानहेतोः प्रतिनिर्मितां तां\nत्वष्ट्रा रिपूणामसुदेहभक्षाम् ।\nभूम्यन्तरिक्षादिजलाशयानि\nप्रसह्य भूतानि निहन्तुमीशाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Made by Tvashtri for Ishana, it fed on the bodies and lives of enemies, and was able to destroy beings on earth, in the sky and in the waters by force."}},{"n":45,"text":"घण्टापताकामणिवज्रभाजं\nवैडूर्यचित्रां तपनीयदण्डाम् ।\nत्वष्ट्रा प्रयत्नान्नियमेन कॢप्तां\nब्रह्मद्विषामन्तकरीममोघाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Adorned with bells, banners, gems and diamonds, bright with cat's-eye, with a golden shaft, made with care and discipline by Tvashtri, unfailing, it was the ender of the haters of the Brahmins."}},{"n":46,"text":"बलप्रयत्नादधिरूढवेगां\nमन्त्रैश्च घोरैरभिमन्त्रयित्वा ।\nससर्ज मार्गेण च तां परेण\nवधाय मद्राधिपतेस्तदानीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Charged with speed by his strength and effort, and consecrated with fearful mantras, he sent it by the best course at that moment to kill the lord of Madra."}},{"n":47,"text":"हतोऽस्यसावित्यभिगर्जमानो\nरुद्रोऽन्तकायान्तकरं यथेषुम् ।\nप्रसार्य बाहुं सुदृढं सुपाणिं\nक्रोधेन नृत्यन्निव धर्मराजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shouting \"You are slain!\" like Rudra hurling an arrow that ends the world at Death himself, Yudhishthira stretched out his arm, firm and well-handed, dancing as it were in rage."}},{"n":48,"text":"तां सर्वशक्त्या प्रहितां स शक्तिं\nयुधिष्ठिरेणाप्रतिवार्यवीर्याम् ।\nप्रतिग्रहायाभिननर्द शल्यः\nसम्यग्घुतामग्निरिवाज्यधाराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that lance, sent with all his strength by Yudhishthira, of irresistible power, came, Shalya roared to receive it, like fire receiving a stream of ghee well poured."}},{"n":49,"text":"सा तस्य मर्माणि विदार्य शुभ्र-\nमुरो विशालं च तथैव वर्म ।\nविवेश गां तोयमिवाप्रसक्ता\nयशो विशालं नृपतेर्दहन्ती ॥","meaning":{"en":"It split his vitals, his bright broad chest and his armor, and entered the earth unchecked like water, burning the king's wide fame."}},{"n":50,"text":"नासाक्षिकर्णास्यविनिःसृतेन\nप्रस्यन्दता च व्रणसंभवेन ।\nसंसिक्तगात्रो रुधिरेण सोऽभू-\nत्क्रौञ्चो यथा स्कन्दहतो महाद्रिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His body was soaked with blood flowing from his nose, eyes, ears and mouth and from the wound, like the great mountain Krauncha struck by Skanda."}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रसार्य बाहू स रथाद्गतो गां\nसंछिन्नवर्मा कुरुनन्दनेन ।\nमहेन्द्रवाहप्रतिमो महात्मा\nवज्राहतं शृङ्गमिवाचलस्य ॥","meaning":{"en":"Spreading his arms, his armor cut by the delight of the Kurus, the great-souled man fell from the chariot to the earth, like Indra's elephant, or like a peak of a mountain struck by lightning."}},{"n":52,"text":"बाहू प्रसार्याभिमुखो धर्मराजस्य मद्रराट् ।\nततो निपतितो भूमाविन्द्रध्वज इवोच्छ्रितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Facing the king of dharma, the king of Madras fell to the ground with arms spread, like a tall banner of Indra."}},{"n":53,"text":"स तथा भिन्नसर्वाङ्गो रुधिरेण समुक्षितः ।\nप्रत्युद्गत इव प्रेम्णा भूम्या स नरपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His whole body split and sprinkled with blood, that bull among men seemed to be met with love by the earth."}},{"n":54,"text":"प्रियया कान्तया कान्तः पतमान इवोरसि ।\nचिरं भुक्त्वा वसुमतीं प्रियां कान्तामिव प्रभुः ।\nसर्वैरङ्गैः समाश्लिष्य प्रसुप्त इव सोऽभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He seemed to fall, like a lover on his beloved's breast, the lord who had long enjoyed the earth as a dear lover, embracing her with all his limbs, as if fast asleep."}},{"n":55,"text":"धर्म्ये धर्मात्मना युद्धे निहतो धर्मसूनुना ।\nसम्यग्घुत इव स्विष्टः प्रशान्तोऽग्निरिवाध्वरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Killed in a lawful fight by the son of Dharma, the righteous-souled, he was like a well-offered sacrificial fire, quenched at the end of a rite."}},{"n":56,"text":"शक्त्या विभिन्नहृदयं विप्रविद्धायुधध्वजम् ।\nसंशान्तमपि मद्रेशं लक्ष्मीर्नैव व्यमुञ्चत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though his heart was split by the lance, his weapons and banner thrown aside, and he was quiet at last, the lord of Madra's glory did not leave him."}},{"n":57,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरश्चापमादायेन्द्रधनुष्प्रभम् ।\nव्यधमद्द्विषतः संख्ये खगराडिव पन्नगान् ।\nदेहासून्निशितैर्भल्लै रिपूणां नाशयन्क्षणात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Yudhishthira took a bow bright as Indra's rainbow and cut down his foes in the battle, as the king of birds cuts down snakes, destroying the bodies and lives of the enemy in a moment with sharp broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततः पार्थस्य बाणौघैरावृताः सैनिकास्तव ।\nनिमीलिताक्षाः क्षिण्वन्तो भृशमन्योन्यमर्दिताः ।\nसंन्यस्तकवचा देहैर्विपत्रायुधजीविताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then your soldiers, covered by Partha's masses of arrows, closed their eyes, crying out, crushing one another, their armor laid aside, their weapons and lives lost with their bodies."}},{"n":59,"text":"ततः शल्ये निपतिते मद्रराजानुजो युवा ।\nभ्रातुः सर्वैर्गुणैस्तुल्यो रथी पाण्डवमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, when Shalya had fallen, the young younger brother of the king of Madras, a chariot-fighter equal to his brother in all virtues, charged the Pandava."}},{"n":60,"text":"विव्याध च नरश्रेष्ठो नाराचैर्बहुभिस्त्वरन् ।\nहतस्यापचितिं भ्रातुश्चिकीर्षुर्युद्धदुर्मदः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That best of men, wild in battle, wishing to avenge his killed brother, hurriedly pierced him with many iron arrows."}},{"n":61,"text":"तं विव्याधाशुगैः षड्भिर्धर्मराजस्त्वरन्निव ।\nकार्मुकं चास्य चिच्छेद क्षुराभ्यां ध्वजमेव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira, the king of dharma, as if in haste, pierced him with six swift arrows and with two razor-arrows cut his bow and his banner."}},{"n":62,"text":"ततोऽस्य दीप्यमानेन सुदृढेन शितेन च ।\nप्रमुखे वर्तमानस्य भल्लेनापाहरच्छिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as he stood in front, he took his head with a bright, strong, sharp broad-headed arrow."}},{"n":63,"text":"सकुण्डलं तद्ददृशे पतमानं शिरो रथात् ।\nपुण्यक्षयमिव प्राप्य पतन्तं स्वर्गवासिनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The head with its earrings was seen falling from the chariot, like a dweller in heaven falling when his merit is spent."}},{"n":64,"text":"तस्यापकृष्टशीर्षं तच्छरीरं पतितं रथात् ।\nरुधिरेणावसिक्ताङ्गं दृष्ट्वा सैन्यमभज्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing his body, its head cut off, fallen from the chariot with its limbs soaked in blood, the army broke."}},{"n":65,"text":"विचित्रकवचे तस्मिन्हते मद्रनृपानुजे ।\nहाहाकारं विकुर्वाणाः कुरवो विप्रदुद्रुवुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that younger brother of the king of Madras, in his wonderful armor, was killed, the Kurus, crying out in dismay, scattered in flight."}},{"n":66,"text":"शल्यानुजं हतं दृष्ट्वा तावकास्त्यक्तजीविताः ।\nवित्रेसुः पाण्डवभयाद्रजोध्वस्तास्तथा भृशम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing Shalya's younger brother killed, your men, giving up on life, trembled in fear of the Pandavas and were badly cast down by the dust."}},{"n":67,"text":"तांस्तथा भज्यतस्त्रस्तान्कौरवान्भरतर्षभ ।\nशिनेर्नप्ता किरन्बाणैरभ्यवर्तत सात्यकिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As those Kauravas broke and fled in terror, best of Bharatas, Shini's grandson Satyaki came against them, showering arrows."}},{"n":68,"text":"तमायान्तं महेष्वासमप्रसह्यं दुरासदम् ।\nहार्दिक्यस्त्वरितो राजन्प्रत्यगृह्णादभीतवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that great archer, irresistible and hard to approach, came on, the son of Hridika, Kritavarman, quickly met him fearlessly."}},{"n":69,"text":"तौ समेतौ महात्मानौ वार्ष्णेयावपराजितौ ।\nहार्दिक्यः सात्यकिश्चैव सिंहाविव मदोत्कटौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Those two great-souled, unconquered Vrishnis, Kritavarman and Satyaki, met like two lions maddened with rut."}},{"n":70,"text":"इषुभिर्विमलाभासैश्छादयन्तौ परस्परम् ।\nअर्चिर्भिरिव सूर्यस्य दिवाकरसमप्रभौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"They covered each other with bright arrows, like two suns shining with their rays."}},{"n":71,"text":"चापमार्गबलोद्धूतान्मार्गणान्वृष्णिसिंहयोः ।\nआकाशे समपश्याम पतंगानिव शीघ्रगान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"We saw in the sky the arrows loosed with the force of the bows of those two lions of the Vrishnis, like swift-flying birds."}},{"n":72,"text":"सात्यकिं दशभिर्विद्ध्वा हयांश्चास्य त्रिभिः शरैः ।\nचापमेकेन चिच्छेद हार्दिक्यो नतपर्वणा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kritavarman pierced Satyaki with ten arrows and his horses with three, and cut his bow with one arrow with bent joints."}},{"n":73,"text":"तन्निकृत्तं धनुः श्रेष्ठमपास्य शिनिपुंगवः ।\nअन्यदादत्त वेगेन वेगवत्तरमायुधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The bull of the Shini line threw aside that cut best bow and quickly took another, swifter weapon."}},{"n":74,"text":"तदादाय धनुः श्रेष्ठं वरिष्ठः सर्वधन्विनाम् ।\nहार्दिक्यं दशभिर्बाणैः प्रत्यविध्यत्स्तनान्तरे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking that best bow, the foremost of all archers pierced Kritavarman in the chest with ten arrows in return."}},{"n":75,"text":"ततो रथं युगेषां च छित्त्वा भल्लैः सुसंयतैः ।\nअश्वांस्तस्यावधीत्तूर्णमुभौ च पार्ष्णिसारथी ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he cut Kritavarman's chariot and its yoke-pole with firmly shot broad-headed arrows, and quickly killed his horses and his two rear guards."}},{"n":76,"text":"मद्रराजे हते राजन्विरथे कृतवर्मणि ।\nदुर्योधनबलं सर्वं पुनरासीत्पराङ्मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the king of Madras was killed and Kritavarman chariotless, O king, all Duryodhana's army again turned its back."}},{"n":77,"text":"तत्परे नावबुध्यन्त सैन्येन रजसा वृते ।\nबलं तु हतभूयिष्ठं तत्तदासीत्पराङ्मुखम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The enemy did not notice it, being wrapped in the dust of the army; the force, mostly slain, was turning away."}},{"n":78,"text":"ततो मुहूर्तात्तेऽपश्यन्रजो भौमं समुत्थितम् ।\nविविधैः शोणितस्रावैः प्रशान्तं पुरुषर्षभ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then after a moment they saw the dust risen from the earth, settled by streams of blood of many kinds, bull among men."}},{"n":79,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो दृष्ट्वा भग्नं स्वबलमन्तिकात् ।\nजवेनापततः पार्थानेकः सर्वानवारयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Duryodhana, seeing his army broken near him, alone held back all the Pandavas as they rushed on swiftly."}},{"n":80,"text":"पाण्डवान्सरथान्दृष्ट्वा धृष्टद्युम्नं च पार्षतम् ।\nआनर्तं च दुराधर्षं शितैर्बाणैरवाकिरत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Pandavas with their chariots, and Dhrishtadyumna son of Prishata, and the invincible Anarta man, Satyaki, he covered them with sharp arrows."}},{"n":81,"text":"तं परे नाभ्यवर्तन्त मर्त्या मृत्युमिवागतम् ।\nअथान्यं रथमास्थाय हार्दिक्योऽपि न्यवर्तत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The enemy could not face him as he came, like men facing Death. Then Kritavarman, taking another chariot, also came back."}},{"n":82,"text":"ततो युधिष्ठिरो राजा त्वरमाणो महारथः ।\nचतुर्भिर्निजघानाश्वान्पत्रिभिः कृतवर्मणः ।\nविव्याध गौतमं चापि षड्भिर्भल्लैः सुतेजनैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Yudhishthira, the great warrior, in haste, killed Kritavarman's horses with four feathered arrows and pierced Kripa the Gautama with six bright broad-headed arrows."}},{"n":83,"text":"अश्वत्थामा ततो राज्ञा हताश्वं विरथीकृतम् ।\nसमपोवाह हार्दिक्यं स्वरथेन युधिष्ठिरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Ashvatthama carried Kritavarman, whose horses the king had killed and who had been left chariotless, away from Yudhishthira in his own chariot."}},{"n":84,"text":"ततः शारद्वतोऽष्टाभिः प्रत्यविध्यद्युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nविव्याध चाश्वान्निशितैस्तस्याष्टाभिः शिलीमुखैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kripa, the son of Sharadvat, struck Yudhishthira back with eight arrows and pierced his horses with eight sharp arrows."}},{"n":85,"text":"एवमेतन्महाराज युद्धशेषमवर्तत ।\nतव दुर्मन्त्रिते राजन्सहपुत्रस्य भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, great king, did the rest of the battle go on, because of the ill counsel of you and your son, O Bharata."}},{"n":86,"text":"तस्मिन्महेष्वासवरे विशस्ते\nसंग्राममध्ये कुरुपुंगवेन ।\nपार्थाः समेताः परमप्रहृष्टाः\nशङ्खान्प्रदध्मुर्हतमीक्ष्य शल्यम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When that best of great archers had been slain in the midst of the battle by the bull of the Kurus, the Pandavas, assembled and exceedingly glad, blew their conches, seeing Shalya dead."}},{"n":87,"text":"युधिष्ठिरं च प्रशशंसुराजौ\nपुरा सुरा वृत्रवधे यथेन्द्रम् ।\nचक्रुश्च नानाविधवाद्यशब्दा-\nन्निनादयन्तो वसुधां समन्तात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The kings praised Yudhishthira, as the gods once praised Indra at the killing of Vritra, and made many kinds of instrument sounds, filling the earth with noise on every side."}}]}]}